@@ -20,6 +20,18 @@ adds no domain surface.
 | R47-C1 | depth | `SKILL.md` `## Queue-drain craft` rule block 24 — the **exactness** matrix over the four round-46 routed instrument defects — and its interpreter `tools/round-47/exact.py` |
 | R47-C2 | calibration | the lane's **current self-assessment** (the last two `## Round N` sections of `SCORECARD.md`) re-derived atom by atom against committed repo state by `tools/round-47/record.py` |
 
+**Freeze amendment A1 (declared before any claim data; the freeze is a series of two, disclosed).**
+The first freeze `5017e1f7299c3a812e87e7950148f54313dd279e` carried a `record.py` clause no reachable
+correction could satisfy: it required a `window` correction's `A..B` pair to already appear in the
+card, while the only window atom in scope names a `<tip>` placeholder — so R47-C2's target was
+unreachable by construction. A1 deletes that clause and nothing else; the **declared freeze is the
+commit that carries this paragraph**, i.e. the first commit whose `tools/round-47/record.py` scores
+the landing's own corrections section. Red-before at the first freeze: the landing corrections
+scored `corrections_bad: [window pair names no atom in scope]`, exit 1
+(`.ufo/waves/round-47/controls/ctl-c2-2-freeze-amendment.json`). No seat had scored a claim and no
+landing had been measured when A1 was made; the two-commit series is disclosed here rather than
+folded, per the round-46 M46-3 finding.
+
 **Causal separability.** R47-C1's counter reads `SKILL.md`, this file's frozen paths,
 `tools/round-47/exact.py` and `tools/round-46/gate.py`; it never reads `SCORECARD.md`.
 R47-C2's counter reads `SCORECARD.md` and the `.ufo/waves/round-*/` dispatch and receipt
